<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bikini Atoll</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bikini Atoll is a ring of coral islands in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a>. In 1946 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> moved its inhabitants to other atolls and began nuclear testing there with Operation Crossroads, followed by 23 nuclear explosions up to 1958, including the Castle Bravo hydrogen bomb test of 1954. Residual radiation has prevented the islanders from returning permanently, and the test site was listed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2010.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bikini-atoll.jpg" alt="Bikini Atoll" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bikini_Atoll_2001-01-14,_Landsat_7_ETM%2B,_bands_3-2-1-8.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
